WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.697
What apps know about you: read your data exports without uploading them.

2
00:00:06.197 --> 00:00:10.992
How to ask Spotify, WhatsApp, Instagram, Google and others for your data,

3
00:00:10.992 --> 00:00:16.181
and how to turn their ZIP files into stats, lists and maps inside your browser.

4
00:00:17.581 --> 00:00:22.146
How to ask for your data. The request is always in the settings, usually

5
00:00:22.146 --> 00:00:24.301
under privacy or your information.

6
00:00:25.601 --> 00:00:27.729
Chats: who talks most, and when.

7
00:00:27.729 --> 00:00:32.515
A WhatsApp export is plain text: a date, a time, a name, a colon and the

8
00:00:32.515 --> 00:00:33.047
message.

9
00:00:34.347 --> 00:00:38.827
Places you have been. Location history is the most sensitive file of all.

10
00:00:40.127 --> 00:00:45.079
Anything else. For services without a tool of their own, Data Export Explorer

11
00:00:45.079 --> 00:00:48.745
opens any export ZIP, guesses which service it came from.

12
00:00:50.045 --> 00:00:53.467
To try it, open WhatsApp Chat Analyzer in OpenFile.

13
00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:57.291
Drop in a file, adjust the settings and press the button.

14
00:00:57.291 --> 00:01:00.712
It all runs on your device, so nothing is uploaded.

15
00:01:03.145 --> 00:01:06.836
Read the full post, with live demos, on the OpenFile blog.
